From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ptyd: send SIGHUP when the master side of a PTY closes

When an SSH session ends, sshd closes the PTY master. The shell on the
slave side was never told; it read EOF, wrote to a dead terminal and
panicked. Like Unix, send SIGHUP (and SIGCONT) to every process group
that was in front on this terminal.
---
diff --git a/ptyd/src/controlterm.rs b/ptyd/src/controlterm.rs
index c0e79088..099de5d5 100644
--- a/ptyd/src/controlterm.rs
+++ b/ptyd/src/controlterm.rs
@@ -28,6 +28,12 @@ impl PtyControlTerm {
     }
 }
 
+impl Drop for PtyControlTerm {
+    fn drop(&mut self) {
+        self.pty.borrow().hangup();
+    }
+}
+
